t criteria weighed against a classmate's goals (shared with permission) and the setting, with constructive feedback. Each item is marked met, partly or not yet. Out: deliberate tone tied to the student's own goals (Level 1). Tools: the style sheet, the revision log, the criteria builder card, Curio Class's own. Free path: a drawn style sheet and a paper or live piece. Once-a-week path: 6 sessions | After unit 10 because the style piece is produced through a planned workflow with conventions bent on purpose; contrast of styles came in unit 9. Before unit 12, whose theme crosses formats | Candidate: a style-blending work by a maker from Africa or the Americas, described and linked | Peking opera faces and Irish folk figures: studied as a film's conventions with their setting; no student wears or paints an opera face or plays a folk figure, and each tradition is told from its own published sources, read first by the agent (a Chinese film archive's or museum's page; an Irish folklore archive's page). Critique talks about the work, never the maker. Hazards and controls: screen breaks, no strobe, recording only with the family's yes. Agent reads: sensitivity; safety (hands-on). |
