MA:Cr1.1.6	Practice chosen creative methods to shape varied aims and fixes for media work.
MA:Cr1.1.7	Apply chosen inventive processes, like prototyping, to make varied ideas and solutions.
MA:Cr1.1.8	Use targeted inventive methods, like thinking in many directions, to produce ideas and fixes.
MA:Cr2.1.6	Organize plans, mockups, and production steps, then critique them against your purpose.
MA:Cr2.1.7	Draft and assess plans, mockups, and production steps for expressive aims and available resources.
MA:Cr2.1.8	Structure and critique workflows and prototypes, weighing intent, resources, and presentation setting.
MA:Cr3.1.6a	Try several approaches to make purposeful content, using principles like point of view.
MA:Cr3.1.6b	Judge how changing elements could achieve intended effects, then refine pieces for the audience.
MA:Cr3.1.7a	Coordinate production steps to merge content for meaning, using principles like narrative structure.
MA:Cr3.1.7b	Improve media pieces by stressing expressive elements suited to their audience and setting.
MA:Cr3.1.8a	Blend content and style conventions through production steps, applying principles such as unity.
MA:Cr3.1.8b	Polish technical quality and highlight chosen style elements to suit purpose, viewers, and setting.
MA:Pr4.1.6	Show how blending several forms and kinds of content backs a piece's core message.
MA:Pr4.1.7	Merge content types and forms into one work with a consistent viewpoint and story.
MA:Pr4.1.8	Merge content types and forms into one work that conveys a theme or idea.
MA:Pr5.1.6a	Build varied art, design, tech, and people skills by performing assigned production roles.
MA:Pr5.1.6b	Develop flexible creativity, for instance by testing constraints, to find solutions.
MA:Pr5.1.6c	Show flexibility using tools in both ordinary and experimental approaches.
MA:Pr5.1.7a	Show growing skills across roles, including solving problems creatively and organizing.
MA:Pr5.1.7b	Show growing creative and adaptive abilities, such as exploring, while developing solutions.
MA:Pr5.1.7c	Adapt tools and methods, both ordinary and experimental, to meet an assigned purpose.
MA:Pr5.1.8a	Show a set range of art, design, tech, and people skills in assigned roles.
MA:Pr5.1.8b	Show creative and adaptive abilities, such as bending conventions, to solve named problems.
MA:Pr5.1.8c	Adapt tools, methods, and content, both ordinary and experimental, to express your intent.
MA:Pr6.1.6a	Analyze presentation formats and complete varied tasks in presenting and distributing media.
MA:Pr6.1.6b	Analyze how a presentation went and what to improve.
MA:Pr6.1.7a	Evaluate presentation formats to decide how to complete presentation and distribution tasks.
MA:Pr6.1.7b	Evaluate presentation results and improvements, considering effects on your own growth.
MA:Pr6.1.8a	Design how media will be presented and distributed through several formats or contexts.
MA:Pr6.1.8b	Evaluate presentation results and put improvements in place, considering personal growth and outside effects.
MA:Re7.1.6a	Name and describe parts of a piece, then analyze how they build meaning.
MA:Re7.1.6b	Name and describe techniques and styles, then analyze how they steer the audience's experience.
MA:Re7.1.7a	Compare and analyze qualities of parts of media pieces and how they relate.
MA:Re7.1.7b	Analyze how techniques and styles combine with personal taste to shape audience experience.
MA:Re7.1.8a	Contrast and analyze qualities of, and links among, parts and styles within media pieces.
MA:Re7.1.8b	Analyze and contrast how techniques and styles steer what audiences feel and intend.
MA:Re8.1.6	Analyze what different media pieces intend, using criteria given to you.
MA:Re8.1.7	Analyze what varied media pieces intend and mean, using criteria you developed.
MA:Re8.1.8	Analyze intent and meaning of varied media pieces, looking at forms and contexts.
MA:Re9.1.6	Choose particular criteria to judge varied media pieces and production steps, giving constructive feedback.
MA:Re9.1.7	Build your own criteria to evaluate media pieces and production steps, with constructive feedback.
MA:Re9.1.8	Judge media pieces and production steps with built criteria, weighing context and goals.
MA:Cn10.1.6a	Find, judge, and draw on inner and outer resources, including research, to create media.
MA:Cn10.1.6b	Show media producing new meanings and experiences, for example around historical events.
MA:Cn10.1.7a	Find, judge, and use varied sources, including strong example works, to guide creating media.
MA:Cn10.1.7b	Explain how media creates new meaning, knowledge, and cultural experiences, for example in learning.
MA:Cn10.1.8a	Find, judge, and use cultural and social knowledge, research, and model works for creation.
MA:Cn10.1.8b	Show how media broadens knowledge and creates cultural experiences, from local to worldwide events.
MA:Cn11.1.6a	Investigate how media connects to identity, history, entertainment, and community or cultural situations.
MA:Cn11.1.6b	Analyze media tools and spaces, using them with fair use, copyright, and ethics.
MA:Cn11.1.7a	Explore how media connects to different purposes and values, like careers and social media.
MA:Cn11.1.7b	Analyze media tools and spaces and use them responsibly, including on social platforms.
MA:Cn11.1.8a	Explain and show how media links to civic, environmental, and community values and purposes.
MA:Cn11.1.8b	Analyze and responsibly use media tools within legal, technological, and virtual-world contexts.

